# Testing And Verification

- Unit-test pure grid, canvas, registry, and geometry helpers directly.
- React tests should follow Testing Library principles: prefer role, label, and visible text queries over implementation details.
- Canvas tests may assert drawing calls when pixels are not practical, but keep behavior-level tests for pointer/selection flows in `App.test.tsx`.
- Do not test third-party libraries. Test how this app wires and responds to them.
- After source changes, run `npm test` and `npm run build` before claiming completion.
- For docs/rules-only changes, verify rule frontmatter, globs, paths, and stale references instead of running unrelated tests.
